            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 68-year-old male admitted on 01/04/2008 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray excluded pneumonia or pneumothorax. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemic respiratory insufficiency. Blood tests showed mild inflammatory markers. He was treated with supplemental oxygen, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Vital signs were monitored continuously. His condition improved steadily, and he was discharged on 02/04/2008 in stable condition. I recommend continued inhaler therapy, early pulmonary rehabilitation referral, and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
